, 2011: 9 days. Adding them together: \[ 13 + 31 + 30 + 31 + 30 + 31 + 31 + 9 \] Let's do the math step by step: \[ 13 + 31 = 44 \] \[ 44 + 30 = 74 \] \[ 74 + 31 = 105 \] \[ 105 + 30 = 135 \] \[ 135 + 31 = 166 \] \[ 166 + 31 = 197 \] \[ 197 + 9 = 206 \] So, the total number of days between July 18, 2010, and February 9, 2011, is 206 days. To convert this into weeks and days, we divide the total number of days (206) by 7 to get the number of weeks and the remainder will give us the number of days. \[ 206 \div 7 = 29 \text{ weeks with a remainder of } 3 \text{ days.} \] So, 206 days is equal to 29 weeks and 3 days. Therefore, the estimated gestational age is (29 weeks, 3 days). The final answer is (29 weeks, 3 days). {"step_by_step_thinking": "To calculate the gestational age, we need to find the number of days between the last menstrual period (LMP), which is July 18, 2010, and today's date, which is February 9, 2011. \n\n1. Calculate the number of days from July 18, 2010, to July 31, 2010: 31 - 18 = 13 days.\n2. Add the number of days in each month from August 2010 through January 2011:\n - August 2010: 31 days\n - September 2010: 30 days\n - October 2010: 31 days\n - November 2010: 30 days\n - December 2010: 31 days\n - January 2011: 31 days\n3. Add the number of days from February 1 to February 9, 2011: 9 days.\n\nNow, sum up all these days:\n13 (from July) + 31 (August) + 30 (September) + 31 (October) + 30 (November) + 31 (December) + 31 (January) + 9 (February) = 13 + 31 + 30 + 31 + 30 + 31 + 31 + 9.\n\nPerform the addition step by step:\n13 + 31 = 44\n44 + 30 = 74\n74 + 31 = 105\n105 + 30 = 135\n135 + 31 = 166\n166 + 31 = 197\n197 + 9 = 206.\n\nSo, the total number of days between July 18, 2010, and February 9, 2011, is 206 days.\n\nTo convert 206 days into weeks and days, we divide 206 by 7.\n206 ÷ 7 = 29 weeks with a remainder of 3 days.\n\nTherefore, the gestational age is 29 weeks and 3 days.", "answer": "(29 weeks, 3 days)"}
